\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-China's yuan hits post-reval low after cbank acts  \b0\par\par\uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2005\par 03:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds dealers', analyst's comments, details)  \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, July 27 (Reuters) - China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the yuan to a post-revaluation low against the dollar in a last-moment burst of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, as Beijing strove to cool speculation that last week's appreciation was the first of many, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan closed at 8.1128 to the dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on its Web site ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.pbc.gov.cn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.pbc.gov.cn }}}\uc2 ), its weakest against the dollar since Beijing rocked world markets by revaluing the yuan last Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  diving into the market in the final minutes of trade, first pushing the yuan to 8.1127, then 8.1128 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 It had been trying to send a message to the market, that it did not want the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen further against the dollar, as many had speculated, they said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  indicated also that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be preparing to allow the yuan to move in a wider range.  \par \par \uc2 "It was a clear \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sent a signal to the market that there will be no more appeciations for now," said a floor dealer with a foreign bank.  \par \par \uc2 "But it wasn't a surprise to us, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had said it would not appreciate the yuan after last week's move."  \par \par \uc2 After keeping the yuan, also known as renminbi, virtually fixed near 8.28 per dollar since 1996, Beijing adjusted its value to 8.11 after trading closed on Thursday and said it would manage it with reference to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its main trading partners.  \par \par \uc2 DOWNPLAYING SPECULATION  \par \par \uc2 To play down speculation of a further revaluation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday that the appreciation did not mean there would be more adjustments.  \par \par \uc2 In Wednesday's trading the yuan firmed to 7.1954 against 100 Japanese yen from 7.2496, and strengthened against the euro to 9.7431 from 9.7709., according to China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The yuan hit a post-revaluation high of 8.1089 on Monday, 39 ticks away from Wednesday's low.  \par \par \uc2 The movements, though tiny by international standards, represent a much wider band than the 2 or 3 pip ranges typically seen before Thursday's revaluation.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the yuan was likely to keep move narrowly in the coming days, but could maintain the momentum of moving a bit wider then the pre-revaluation period.  \par \par \uc2 Outside of China, analysts noted that the dollar had strengthened against the yen and the won on Wednesday -- which might also explain the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to nudge the yuan lower against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the move in dollar/yuan had been so small, however, that it suggested the dollar was a large component of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reference basket for the yuan.  \par \par \uc2 "They \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  so aggressively to push dollar/\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a weaker close, and that is consistent with a view that they are targeting a nominal effective exchange rate," said John Cairns, head of research at IDEAglobal in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 "We have to watch over time and see if that trend continues." (Additional reporting by Vidya Ranganathan in Singapore)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-YUAN (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050727e17r0014r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
