\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr recovers as attention turns to rate rises  \b0\par\par\uc2 499 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2005\par 11:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, July 27 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar rebounded late on Wednesday as the market turned away from speculation about the yuan and focused on expectations for an interest rate rise next week.  \par \par \uc2 "We've seen some position adjustment ahead of the month-end and the FOMC meeting next week," a dealer said. "The market expects a U.S. rate hike of 25 basis points that Hong Kong will probably follow."  \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar <HKD=> strengthened to 7.7772/74 to the U.S. dollar late on Wednesday from 7.7777/78 late on Tuesday and after falling to 7.7793/97 by mid-morning.  \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.75-7.85 to the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is often used as a proxy for the Chinese yuan and in morning trade continued to be dominated by comments from China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday saying it had no intention to further revalue the yuan.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the final minutes of yuan trading on Wednesday to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fresh post-revaluation lows and send a further signal that it did not want the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate further for now, dealers in Shanghai said.  \par \par \uc2 In Hong Kong, traders had already switched their attention to U.S. economic data due over the next few days, including second-quarter gross domestic product on Friday. The data is expected to confirm that the U.S. economy remains healthy and raise expectations the Federal Reserve will lift interest rates when the Federal Open Market Committee meets next week.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong tends to track U.S. rate moves because of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 One-year interbank rates edged up to 3.66/3.86 in late trade from 3.50/3.70 late on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The discount on one-year Hong Kong dollar forwards <HKD1Y=> narrowed to 290/270 pips by late trade, from 306/286 pips late on Tuesday but slightly wider than 275/255 in mid-morning.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                  Close          Morning       Previous Close\par                  At 0924 GMT    At 0315 GMT   At 0853 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>    7.7772/73      7.7793/97     7.7777/78\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month         -35/-30        -31/-26       -39/-34\par  Six-month          -106/-96        -97/-87      -115/-105\par  One-year           -295/-280      -275/-255     -306/-286\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight           2.85/2.90      2.85/3.25     2.95/3.10\par  Three-month         3.39/3.59      3.41/3.54     3.35/3.55\par  Six-month           3.53/3.73      3.50/3.70     3.50/3.70\par  One-year            3.66/3.86      3.73/3.78     3.50/3.70\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on Reuters contributor page <FWEN>.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG-FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|Z|RBN|ABN|M|E|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050727e17r0013v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
