\par\par \b \uc2 TAKE A LOOK-China revalues yuan, plays down chance of more moves  \b0\par\par\uc2 605 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2005\par 16:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 China revalued its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and scrapped the yuan's peg to the U.S. dollar last week in what was widely seen as first step in a series of long anticipated reforms.  \par \par \uc2 The reforms announced on Thursday sent shockwaves through financial markets, but their impact has started to fade and on Tuesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  played down the prospect of further revaluations.  \par \par \uc2 The new yuan rate revalues the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 2.1 percent to a midpoint of 8.11 per U.S. dollar. Beijing tied the yuan to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and says it will let the yuan rise or fall by 1.5 percent a day against \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  other than the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 For Reuters stories on the move plus reaction and analysis, double click on the codes within brackets.  \par \par \uc2 MAIN STORIES > China plays down chance of more yuan moves [ID:nPEK359143] > Revaluation buys time, no panacea-China cbanker[ID:nPEK342815] > China yuan move an "initial" step -PBOC head [ID:nPEK329845] > China says bets on bigger yuan rise unrealistic[ID:nPEK328629]   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par > China unveils detailed yuan trading limits     [ID:nPEK315705]\par > POLL-Yuan seen up 4% vs dollar by mid-06       [ID:nL25485001]\par > TEXT-July 21 cbank statement on yuan           [ID:nL21684669]\par > TEXT-July 26 statement on yuan revaluation     [ID:nPEK331516]\par > ANALYSTS' VIEW 2-China statement on yuan       [ID:nPEK357577]\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LATEST ANALYSES/STORIES > Why should China join the deluxe economy club [ID:nL25380409] > Fundamentals, 