\par\par \b \uc2 TAKE A LOOK-China revalues yuan, adopts basket  \b0\par\par\uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 2005\par 16:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 China revalued its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and scrapped the yuan's peg to the U.S. dollar last week in what the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said was first step in a series of reforms.  \par \par \uc2 The new yuan rate revalues the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 2.1 percent to a midpoint of 8.11 per U.S. dollar. Beijing tied the yuan to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and says it will let the yuan rise or fall by 1.5 percent a day against \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  other than the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Although the eagerly anticipated reforms announced on Thursday sent shockwaves through financial markets, their impact had started to fade on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 For Reuters stories on the move plus reaction and analysis, double click on the codes within brackets.  \par \par \uc2 MAIN STORIES > Revaluation buys time, no cure-all-China c.banker [nPEK342815]   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par > China cbank to be first with daily yuan close     [nSHA355041]\par > China yuan move an "initial" step -PBOC head      [nPEK329845]\par > S&P says yuan move could boost region's economies   [nWLB4653]\par > China says bets on bigger yuan rise unrealistic[ID:nPEK328629]\par > China unveils detailed yuan trading limits     [ID:nPEK315705]\par > POLL-Yuan seen appreciating 4% vs dollar by mid-06[nL25485001]\par > FACTBOX-What China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  basket may look like [ID:nSP243281]\par > TEXT-China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  statement on yuan      [ID:nL21684669]\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LATEST ANALYSES/STORIES > Why shou