\par\par \b \uc2 Taiwan dollar softens as yuan fever subsides  \b0\par\par\uc2 460 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 2005\par 03:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates with mid-morning rates, details)  \par \par \uc2 TAIPEI, July 25 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> retreated from a three-week high on Monday as investors stepped back to ponder the implications of China's yuan <CNY=CFXS> revaluation, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar weakened to T$31.720 to the U.S. dollar by 0215 GMT after opening at T$31.680. On Friday, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had hit an intraday peak of T$31.550 -- its highest intraday level since June 30 -- before ending at T$31.648.  \par \par \uc2 Volume fell sharply to US$218 million after an hour and 15 minutes from the previous session's US$431 million.  \par \par \uc2 "Yuan fever has subsided for the time being, especially judging from the yen's levels," said a dealer in Taipei. "But the falls in the Taiwan dollar will be limited because the won didn't move very much at the open."  \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar usually tracks the yen <JPY=> and the won's <KRW=KFTC><KRW=> movements as Japan is the island's largest source of imports, while South Korea is a close competitor in exports.  \par \par \uc2 Zhou Xiaochuan, China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, said on Saturday the yuan's revaluation was an initial step whose benefits outweighed its drawbacks, two days after the government appreciated the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 2.1 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese yen fell to 111.62/65 against the U.S. dollar in the morning from 111.30 in late U.S. trade on Friday. It had surged to 109.87 on Thursday after China's long-anticipated announcement.  \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won lost 0.34 percent to 1,024.8 to the U.S. dollar after opening slightly lower as a yuan-inspired rally faded, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the market to buy U.S. dollars this morning, but the amount was not significant," said a second dealer in Taipei.  \par \par \uc2 Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which favours a weak Taiwan dollar as it helps in maintaining the island's export competitiveness, often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth excessive volatility in the market.  \par \par \uc2 After \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced its yuan revaluation on Thursday, George Chou, director general of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  department, said it would stick to its longstanding policy of ensuring "the dynamic stability" of the Taiwan dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , like many of its counterparts in Asia, had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily on Friday to prevent the Taiwan dollar from firming too much.  \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan unit weakened to T$31.722 to the U.S. dollar on the smaller Cosmos exchange <TWD=COSM> from Friday's close of T$31.638.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-TAIWAN-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|Z|RBN|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050725e17p0005s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
