\par\par \b \uc2 Special Summary: China, Malaysia Abandon  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Pegs  \b0\par\par\uc2 1,536 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2005\par 09:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 China and Malaysia have ended their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pegs and will allow a managed float against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones Newswires' coverage can be found by searching on the code M/CNY and M/MYR. Here is a summary of the main stories about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -peg changes.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China Abandons \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Peg, Revalues Yuan 2% Higher    \f28 \par \par \uc2 In a long-awaited move, China abandoned its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg Thursday and said it would allow the yuan to trade against a basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a so-called managed float regime.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China: Non-USD CNY Pairs To Have 1.5% Limit On Each Side    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China on Friday announced a daily trading limit of 1.5% on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  other than the U.S. dollar that are traded against the yuan. The range is wider than the 0.3% daily trading limit China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set for the main dollar-yuan pair, announced late Thursday. The limits take effect immediately.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Malaysia Severs Ringgit's Link To US \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 In lockstep with China, Malaysia announced that it was abandoning its almost 7-year-old \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg to the dollar in favor of a managed float, a move some bankers and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  specialists suggest could provide the domestic economy with at least a short-term boost.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Japan Tanigaki: China Revaluation 'A Starting Point'    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki on Friday said China's move to revalue its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was a "starting point" on the way to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reform. "CNY8.11 (to the dollar) is merely a result of initial action," Tanigaki said. "I think the yuan rate will move according to the basket system."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Japan Hosoda: Don't See Impact On Japan Econ Of Yuan Move    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's top government spokesman said Friday that China's revaluation of the yuan is unlikely to have a big impact on Japan's economy. Chief Cabinet Secretary Hiroyuki Hosoda praised Beijing's steps to make the yuan more flexible, but said that he would also welcome further yuan-policy reform.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S Korea Fin Min: Yuan Won't Affect USD/KRW Much - Report    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Minister of Finance and Economy Han Duck-Soo said Friday the stronger yuan won't affect the Korean won against the U.S. dollar much, and reiterated the government will act if there is volatility in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, according to online news provider edaily.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Australia Acting PM: China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Move Good For Exports    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mark Vaile, Australia's acting prime minister and trade minister, said that China's decision to revalue the yuan is a plus for Australian exports and international markets. "China is Australia's second-largest export market and the revaluation of the renminbi will make Australian exports cheaper, having a positive impact especially on resources and agriculture products."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Yuan Move May Be Long-Term Neutral For China Oil Demand    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  revaluation may result in a short-term increase in Chinese oil demand, but in the longer term the economic cooling expected from the change is expected to be largely neutral for its oil consumption and for oil prices. A marginally stronger yuan is also unlikely to boost China National Offshore Oil Corp. Ltd.'s high-profile bid for U.S. oil company Unocal Corp.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par The Markets: \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA:Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rally On China, Ctrl Bks Active    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rallied early Friday, but suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by some central banks will likely cap further rises as monetary authorities worry that an excessive rise in their country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will hurt exports. Uncertainty over whether the yuan revaluation is the first of many or a one-time move will also hold back Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par USD/CNY Spot At 8.1106 At 0515 GMT Vs 8.1100 Open  \par  \par Malaysia KLCI Opens Up 1.8% After Ringgit Unpegging    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysian shares opened higher Friday, with the weighted Composite Index of 100 blue-chip stocks up 1.8%, or 16.16 points, to 938.10 in early trading.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =USD/MYR Slips,Short-End Malaysia Bonds Dive On Unpegging   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Malaysia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the continued exclusion of offshore players Friday helped keep the dollar's fall against the ringgit modest a day after the country embraced a managed float system and dropped its 7-year-old fixed-rate regime.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Headlines In The Past Hour \par  \par =China's Yuan Revaluation Buys Firms Political Capital  \par  \par Yuan Revaluation To Boost Natural Rubber Demand - Traders  \par  \par ADB: Yuan Move To Cut China '06 GDP By 0.25-0.5 Pct Pt  \par  \par  \par Other Market Stories: \par  \par =China Revaluation Dents Japan Stocks; No Steep Fall Seen \par =INTERVIEW: China Yuan Impact On Treasurys Limited - CIBC \par Euro/Yuan At 9.9641 At 0330 GMT Fri Vs 10.0641 Thu \par US Dollar Down At MYR3.7900 After MYR Unpegging \par Hong Kong Dollar/Yuan Opens At 1.0638 Vs 1.0638 Thu \par Yen Opens At CNY7.3000 Per 100 Yen Vs 7.3664 Thu \par China Sets JPY/CNY Ctrl Pt 7.3327 Per Y100; 7.3664 Thu \par China Sets EUR/CNY Ctrl Pt 9.8609 Vs 10.0641 Thu Close \par Shanghai Index +0.7% At 1028.14 At 0142 GMT On CNY Move \par USD/SGD At 1.6578 Vs 1.6565 As MAS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -Dealers \par =Australian Dollar Rallies After \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Moves On Yuan \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Govt Bonds On Bourse Open Mostly Dn After Revalue \par =FOCUS: Yuan Revaluation Seen Too Small To Impact Metals \par Canada Afternoon: C$ Higher After Chinese Revaluation \par US Swaps: Spreads Widen As Tsys Fall On China Revaluation \par Yuan Revaluation Short Term Negative For Mortgage Bonds \par Chinese Companies' ADRs Move Up On Yuan Revaluation \par China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Revaluation To Boost HK, China-Related Shrs \par China Yuan Revaluation Likely To Help Chinese Stocks, Bonds \par India Rupee May Add To Gains After Yuan Revaluation \par Malaysia Econ, Markets May Gain From Unpegged Ringgit \par Stronger Yuan A Blow To Argentina's Weak Peso Policy \par  \par Reaction Stories From Around The World \par  \par American Malaysian Chamber Of Commerce Backs MYR Move \par Greenspan: China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Move `Is A Good First Step' \par Japan Takenaka:Yuan Move Desirable For China,Global Econ \par METI Nakagawa: China Yuan Move Mixed Impact On Japan Econ \par Japan Bank Min Ito: China Move 1st Step Toward \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Reform \par Korea Fin Min:To Monitor \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Mkt, To Fully Respond-Report \par Tsy's Snow: China Move "Important Step" For World Economy \par UK Brown: China Yuan Revaluation To Aid Stability, Growth \par FOCUS: Euro Policy-Makers, Cos Hail China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Move \par IMF: China Should Use Full Scope Of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Flexibility \par BOJ: Highly Appreciate China's Decision On Yuan \par Japan MOF Watanabe Welcomes Chinese Yuan Revaluation \par Japan Tanigaki: Welcome China's Decision On Yuan-Kyodo \par Yuan Move A Plus For Brazil, But Little Immediate Impact \par OECD: China's Yuan Move To Support Rapid Growth \par Singapore MAS: Yuan Revualation Won't Have Major Impact \par Thai Ctrl Banker: Yuan Change Good For China, World, Baht \par Taiwan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : No Change To \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Policy \par Philippine Ctrl Bk Expects Peso Gain On Yuan Revaluation \par China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Move Seen Benefiting Argentina's Farmers \par US Tsy Official: No Big Impact On Tsy Mkt From China Move \par  \par Commentary: \par  \par =ASIA ECONOMY WATCH: China, Asian Econs Likely Resilient   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's move is unlikely to dent significantly the country's strong economic growth, which means that Asian economies also are likely to remain resilient, analysts say. The impact depends on whether Thursday's move is followed by further revaluations, and economists are divided as to the likelihood and timing of more adjustments.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =ASIA DEBT: Stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  To Mean Bond Gains Going Forward   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bonds fell early Friday in a kneejerk response to China's surprise revaluation of the yuan, but recovered quickly in anticipation that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation in the region will stave off interest rate hikes. Stronger Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are also ultimately likely to help those countries - like the Philippines, Indonesia, Thailand and China - which have local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  revenues and large U.S. dollar-denominated liabilities.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =POINT OF VIEW: China's Yuan Move To Help Its M&A In U.S.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's modest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  revaluation might have an outsized impact on Chinese companies' ability to execute takeovers in the U.S. The move might weaken U.S. Congressional and other opposition enough to allow future Chinese company attempts to buy U.S. counterparts to attain a greater degree of economic normalcy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VIEW: China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Reform Begins To Crawl   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reform of China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  system picked up speed Thursday - it's now moving at a crawl.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That won't be fast enough a pace to satisfy the harshest U.S. critics of Chinese policy, but it will probably win the Chinese government more time in which to take bigger and stronger strides towards \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flexibility.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =BIG PICTURE: China's Yuan Move No Panacea For Deficit   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chairman Mao is credited with saying the longest journey begins with the first step. On Thursday, the People's Bank of China took the first step on a very long journey when it announced an adjustment to the yuan's exchange rate value.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VIEW: China Move Hits \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Market Where It Hurts   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For many \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  speculators and investors, China's revaluation of the yuan added a painful punctuation to what has been a problematic time. [ 22-07-05 0700GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050722e17m000am\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
