\par\par \b \uc2 Special Summary: China, Malaysia Abandon  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Pegs  \b0\par\par\uc2 1,679 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2005\par 06:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 China and Malaysia have ended their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pegs and will allow a managed float against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones Newswires' coverage can be found by searching on the code M/CNY and M/MYR. Here is a summary of the main stories about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -peg changes.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China Abandons \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Peg, Revalues Yuan 2% Higher  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 In a long-awaited move, China abandoned its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg Thursday and said it would allow the yuan to trade against a basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a so-called managed float regime.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China: Non-USD CNY Pairs To Have 1.5% Limit On Each Side  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China on Friday announced a daily trading limit of 1.5% on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  other than the U.S. dollar that are traded against the yuan. The range is wider than the 0.3% daily trading limit China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set for the main dollar-yuan pair, announced late Thursday. The limits take effect immediately.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Malaysia Severs Ringgit's Link To US \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 In lockstep with China, Malaysia announced that it was abandoning its almost seven-year-old \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg to the dollar in favor of a managed float, a move some bankers and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  specialists suggest could provide the domestic economy with at least a short-term boost.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Japan Tanigaki: China Revaluation 'A Starting Point'  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki on Friday said China's move to revalue its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was a "starting point" on the way to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reform.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "CNY 8.11 (to the dollar) is merely a result of initial action," Tanigaki told reporters at a regular press conference. "I think the yuan rate will move according to the basket system," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Japan Hosoda: Don't See Impact On Japan Econ Of Yuan Move  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's top government spokesman said Friday that China's revaluation of the yuan is unlikely to have a big impact on Japan's economy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chief Cabinet Secretary Hiroyuki Hosoda praised Beijing's steps to make the yuan more flexible, but said that he would also welcome further yuan-policy reform.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S Korea Fin Min: Yuan Won't Affect USD/KRW Much - Report    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Minister of Finance and Economy Han Duck-Soo said Friday the stronger yuan won't affect the Korean won against the U.S. dollar much, and reiterated the government will act if there is volatility in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, according to online news provider edaily.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Australia Acting PM: China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Move Good For Exports  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mark Vaile, Australia's acting prime minister and trade minister, said that China's decision to revalue the yuan is a plus for Australian exports and international markets.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "China is Australia's second largest export market and the revaluation of the renminbi will make Australian exports cheaper, having a positive impact especially on resources and agriculture products," Vaile said in a statement.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par The Markets: \par  \par USD/CNY Opens At 8.11 After China's Revaluation  \par  The dollar began trading at CNY8.11 Friday, according to the China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Trading System. By 0145 GMT, the dollar had risen to CNY8.1105, the CFETS showed. \par  \par Malaysia KLCI Opens Up 1.8% After Ringgit Unpegging  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysian shares opened higher Friday, with the weighted Composite Index of 100 blue-chip stocks up 1.8%, or 16.16 points, to 938.10 in early trading.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US Dollar Down At MYR3.7900 After MYR Unpegging  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Malaysian ringgit strengthened by 0.3% against the U.S. dollar Friday. The U.S. dollar was trading at 3.7900 against the ringgit in early trading, slightly weaker than the MYR3.80 level it was pegged at since 1998.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Treasurys Endure Torrid Session After China Revalues  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasurys suffered a torrid bout of selling after China finally enacted a long-awaited revaluation of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the yuan, and Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan completed his second day of bullish testimony on the economy before Congress.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : Dollar Falls, Yen Spikes On Yuan Revaluation  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen and other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spiked against the dollar and the euro Thursday, as China surprised \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets by revaluing its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Headlines In The Past Hour \par Euro/Yuan At 9.9641 At 0330 GMT Fri Vs 10.0641 Thu  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA:Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rally On China, Ctrl Bks Active  \par  \par American Malaysian Chamber Of Commerce Backs MYR Move  \par  \par Other Market Stories: \par  \par US Dollar Down At MYR3.7900 After MYR Unpegging \par Hong Kong Dollar/Yuan Opens At 1.0638 Vs 1.0638 Thu \par Yen Opens At CNY7.3000 Per 100 Yen Vs 7.3664 Thu \par China Sets JPY/CNY Ctrl Pt 7.3327 Per Y100; 7.3664 Thu \par China Sets EUR/CNY Ctrl Pt 9.8609 Vs 10.0641 Thu Close \par Shanghai Index +0.7% At 1028.14 At 0142 GMT On CNY Move \par USD/SGD At 1.6578 Vs 1.6565 As MAS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -Dealers \par =Australian Dollar Rallies After \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Moves On Yuan \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Govt Bonds On Bourse Open Mostly Dn After Revalue \par =FOCUS: Yuan Revaluation Seen Too Small To Impact Metals \par Canada Afternoon: C$ Higher After Chinese Revaluation \par US Swaps: Spreads Widen As Tsys Fall On China Revaluation \par Yuan Revaluation Short Term Negative For Mortgage Bonds \par Chinese Companies' ADRs Move Up On Yuan Revaluation \par China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Revaluation To Boost HK, China-Related Shrs \par China Yuan Revaluation Likely To Help Chinese Stocks, Bonds \par India Rupee May Add To Gains After Yuan Revaluation \par Malaysia Econ, Markets May Gain From Unpegged Ringgit \par Stronger Yuan A Blow To Argentina's Weak Peso Policy \par  \par Reaction Stories From Around The World \par  \par G