\par\par \b \uc2 Special Summary: China, Malaysia Abandon  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Pegs  \b0\par\par\uc2 1,491 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2005\par 04:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 China and Malaysia have ended their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pegs and will allow a managed float against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones Newswires' coverage can be found by searching on the code M/CNY and M/MYR. Here is a summary of the main stories about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -peg changes.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China Abandons \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Peg, Revalues Yuan 2% Higher  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 In a long-awaited move, China abandoned its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg Thursday and said it would allow the yuan to trade against a basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a so-called managed float regime.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Malaysia Severs Ringgit's Link To US \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 In lockstep with China, Malaysia announced that it was abandoning its almost seven-year-old \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg to the dollar in favor of a managed float, a move some bankers and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  specialists suggest could provide the domestic economy with at least a short-term boost.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Japan Tanigaki: China Revaluation 'A Starting Point'  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki on Friday said China's move to revalue its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was a "starting point" on the way to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reform.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "CNY 8.11 (to the dollar) is merely a result of initial action," Tanigaki told reporters at a regular press conference. "I think the yuan rate will move according to the basket system," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Japan Hosoda: Don't See Impact On Japan Econ Of Yuan Move  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's top government spokesman said Friday that China's revaluation of the yuan is unlikely to have a big impact on Japan's economy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chief Cabinet Secretary Hiroyuki Hosoda praised Beijing's steps to make the yuan more flexible, but said that he would also welcome further yuan-policy reform.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S Korea Fin Min: Yuan Won't Affect USD/KRW Much - Report    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Minister of Finance and Economy Han Duck-Soo said Friday the stronger yuan won't affect the Korean won against the U.S. dollar much, and reiterated the government will act if there is volatility in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, according to online news provider edaily.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Australia Acting PM: China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Move Good For Exports  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mark Vaile, Australia's acting prime minister and trade minister, said that China's decision to revalue the yuan is a plus for Australian exports and international markets.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "China is Australia's second largest export market and the revaluation of the renminbi will make Australian exports cheaper, having a positive impact especially on resources and agriculture products," Vaile said in a statement.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Reaction Stories From Around The World \par Greenspan: China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Move `Is A Good First Step' \par Japan Takenaka:Yuan Move Desirable For China,Global Econ \par METI Nakagawa: China Yuan Move Mixed Impact On Japan Econ \par Japan Bank Min Ito: China Move 1st Step Toward \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Reform \par Korea Fin Min:To Monitor \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Mkt, To Fully Respond-Report \par World Governments, Central Banks Hail China Revaluation \par US Officials Welcome Yuan Revaluation As Good First Step \par US Tsy Snow Welcomes China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Move \par Tsy's Snow: China Move "Important Step" For World Economy \par ECB Trichet: Chinese Yuan Decision Is Welcome \par G7 Fin Mins Welcome China Yuan Move \par UK Brown: China Yuan Revaluation To Aid Stability, Growth \par FOCUS: Euro Policy-Makers, Cos Hail China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Move \par IMF: China Should Use Full Scope Of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Flexibility \par BOJ: Highly Appreciate China's Decision On Yuan \par Japan MOF Watanabe Welcomes Chinese Yuan Revaluation \par Japan Tanigaki: Welcome China's Decision On Yuan-Kyodo \par German BGA: China's Yuan Revaluation Only A First Step \par    -German BGA Group: Further Yuan Revaluation Steps Needed \par Germany's Eichel Welcomes China's Yuan Revaluation \par French Fin Min: Yuan Revaluation In Line With G7 Wishes \par Yuan Move A Plus For Brazil, But Little Immediate Impact \par OECD: China's Yuan Move To Support Rapid Growth \par Singapore MAS: Yuan Revualation Won't Have Major Impact \par Thai Ctrl Banker: Yuan Change Good For China, World, Baht \par Taiwan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : No Change To \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Policy \par Philippine Ctrl Bk Expects Peso Gain On Yuan Revaluation \par China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Move Seen Benefiting Argentina's Farmers \par US Tsy Official: No Big Impact On Tsy Mkt From China Move \par  \par  \par Other Stories: \par  \par Full Text Of China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Statement On Yuan Change \par RATINGS WATCH: China Upgrade Factored In Revaluation \par China PBOC: Raises Upper Limit For USD, HKD Deposit Rates \par =UPDATE: Hong Kong Still Satisified With Peg System \par US Stks Outlook: China's Yuan Move Offers Opportunities \par US Cos Likely To Remain Indebted To China Despite Reval \par China's Float Of Yuan Could Increase Tech Part Costs \par WSJ: US Specialist On China Sees Good And Bad In Yuan Move \par BIS: Yuan Move A Welcome Step Towards \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Flexibility \par US Sen Graham: China Move Achieves Much Of What Was Sought \par US Sens Schumer,Graham Suspend Vote On China Tariff Bill \par US Sen: China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Move A 'Good 1st Step...Baby Step' \par Sen Grassley: China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Move 'By No Means End Of The Road' \par US Cos May Seen Higher Funding Costs On China Yuan Move \par Retailers Still Have Options After China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Move \par China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Float May Level M&A Playing Field In US \par  \par The Markets: \par  \par USD/CNY Opens At 8.11 After China's Revaluation  \par  The dollar began trading at CNY8.11 Friday, according to the China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Trading System. By 0145 GMT, the dollar had risen to CNY8.1105, the CFETS showed. \par  \par Malaysia KLCI Opens Up 1.8% After Ringgit Unpegging  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysian shares opened higher Friday, with the weighted Composite Index of 100 blue-chip stocks up 1.8%, or 16.16 points, to 938.10 in early trading.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US Dollar Down At MYR3.7900 After MYR Unpegging  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Malaysian ringgit strengthened by 0.3% against the U.S. dollar Friday. The U.S. dollar was trading at 3.7900 against the ringgit in early trading, slightly weaker than the MYR3.80 level it was pegged at since 1998.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Treasurys Endure Torrid Session After China Revalues \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasurys suffered a torrid bout of selling after China finally enacted a long-awaited revaluation of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the yuan, and Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan completed his second day of bullish testimony on the economy before Congress.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : Dollar Falls, Yen Spikes On Yuan Revaluation \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen and other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spiked against the dollar and the euro Thursday, as China surprised \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets by revaluing its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par Other Market Stories: \par US Dollar Down At MYR3.7900 After MYR Unpegging \par Shanghai Index +0.7% At 1028.14 At 0142 GMT On CNY Move \par USD/SGD At 1.6578 Vs 1.6565 As MAS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -Dealers \par =Australian Dollar Rallies After \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Moves On Yuan \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Govt Bonds On Bourse Open Mostly Dn After Revalue \par =FOCUS: Yuan Revaluation Seen Too Small To Impact Metals \par Canada Afternoon: C$ Higher After Chinese Revaluation \par US Swaps: Spreads Widen As Tsys Fall On China Revaluation \par Yuan Revaluation Short Term Negative For Mortgage Bonds \par Chinese Companies' ADRs Move Up On Yuan Revaluation \par China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Revaluation To Boost HK, China-Related Shrs \par China Yuan Revaluation Likely To Help Chinese Stocks, Bonds \par India Rupee May Add To Gains After Yuan Revaluation \par Malaysia Econ, Markets May Gain From Unpegged Ringgit \par Stronger Yuan A Blow To Argentina's Weak Peso Policy \par  \par  \par Commentary: \par  \par =POINT OF VIEW: China's Yuan Move To Help Its M&A In U.S. \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's modest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  revaluation might have an outsized impact on Chinese companies' ability to execute takeovers in the U.S. The move might weaken U.S. Congressional and other opposition enough to allow future Chinese company attempts to buy U.S. counterparts to attain a greater degree of economic normalcy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VIEW: China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Reform Begins To Crawl \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reform of China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  system picked up speed Thursday - it's now moving at a crawl.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That won't be fast enough a pace to satisfy the harshest U.S. critics of Chinese policy, but it will probably win the Chinese government more time in which to take bigger and stronger strides towards \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flexibility.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =BIG PICTURE: China's Yuan Move No Panacea For Deficit \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chairman Mao is credited with saying the longest journey begins with the first step. On Thursday, the People's Bank of China took the first step on a very long journey when it announced an adjustment to the yuan's exchange rate value.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VIEW: China Move Hits \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Market Where It Hurts \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For many \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  speculators and investors, China's revaluation of the yuan added a painful punctuation to what has been a problematic time.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Other Commentary: \par =GLOBAL YIELD: It's Small, But China Move Packs Punch \par =ECB Watch:China Yuan Move Makes ECB Rate Cut Less Likely \par =AWSJ: Yuan Revaluation Gives China Monetary Flexibility \par =AWSJ: China Yuan Move May Spur Pressure For More Change \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Focus: Speculation On Yuan Will Increase Now \par =FOCUS: Yuan Move Has Limited Impact On Oil Markets \par =CHARTING AMERICAS: Dollar Continues Its Own Revaluation \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VIEW: Chinese Revaluation Short-Term Boost For C$ \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 22-07-05 0200GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050722e17m0002c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
