\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Special Summary: China, Malaysia Abandon  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Pegs  \b0\par\par\uc2 1,549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2005\par 10:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 China and Malaysia have ended their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pegs and will allow a managed float against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones Newswires' coverage can be found by searching on the code M/CNY and M/MYR. Here is a summary of the main stories about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -peg changes. China Abandons \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Peg, Revalues Yuan 2% Higher  \par \par \uc2 In a long-awaited move, China abandoned its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg Thursday and said it would allow the yuan to trade against a basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a so-called managed float regime. China: Non-USD CNY Pairs To Have 1.5% Limit On Each Side  \par \par \uc2 China on Friday announced a daily trading limit of 1.5% on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  other than the U.S. dollar that are traded against the yuan. The range is wider than the 0.3% daily trading limit China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set for the main dollar-yuan pair, announced late Thursday. The limits take effect immediately. Malaysia Severs Ringgit's Link To US \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 In lockstep with China, Malaysia announced that it was abandoning its almost 7-year-old \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to the dollar in favor of a managed float, a move some bankers and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  specialists suggest could provide the domestic economy with at least a short-term boost. Japan Tanigaki: China Revaluation 'A Starting Point'  \par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki on Friday said China's move to revalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a "starting point" on the way to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform. "CNY8.11 (to the dollar) is merely a result of initial action," Tanigaki said. "I think the yuan rate will move according to the basket system." Japan Hosoda: Don't See Impact On Japan Econ Of Yuan Move  \par \par \uc2 Japan's top government spokesman said Friday that China's revaluation of the yuan is unlikely to have a big impact on Japan's economy. Chief Cabinet Secretary Hiroyuki Hosoda praised Beijing's steps to make the yuan more flexible, but said that he would also welcome further yuan-policy reform. S Korea Fin Min: Yuan Won't Affect USD/KRW Much - Report  \par \par \uc2 South Korea's Minister of Finance and Economy Han Duck-Soo said Friday the stronger yuan won't affect the Korean won against the U.S. dollar much, and reiterated the government will act if there is volatility in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, according to online news provider edaily. Australia Acting PM: China \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Move Good For Exports  \par \par \uc2 Mark Vaile, Australia's acting prime minister and trade minister, said that China's decision to revalue the yuan is a plus for Australian exports and international markets. "China is Australia's second-largest export market and the revaluation of the renminbi will make Australian exports cheaper, having a positive impact especially on resources and agriculture products." Yuan Move May Be Long-Term Neutral For China Oil Demand  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revaluation may result in a short-term increase in Chinese oil demand, but in the longer term the economic cooling expected from the change is expected to be largely neutral for its oil consumption and for oil prices. A marginally stronger yuan is also unlikely to boost China National Offshore Oil Corp. Ltd.'s high-profile bid for U.S. oil company Unocal Corp. The Markets: US Dollar/Yuan Closes At 8.1111 Vs 8.1100 Open Yen Closes At CNY7.3059 Per 100 Yen Vs 7.3000 Open Euro/Yuan Closes At 10.0141 Vs 10.0641 Open Malaysia KLCI Opens Up 1.8% After Ringgit Unpegging  \par \par \uc2 Malaysian shares opened higher Friday, with the weighted Composite Index of 100 blue-chip stocks up 1.8%, or 16.16 points, to 938.10 in early trading. =USD/MYR Slips,Short-End Malaysia Bonds Dive On Unpegging  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the continued exclusion of offshore players Friday helped keep the dollar's fall against the ringgit modest a day after the country embraced a managed float system and dropped its 7-year-old fixed-rate regime. =China's Yuan Revaluation Buys Firms Political Capital  \par \par \uc2 China's revaluation of the yuan should make it cheaper for Chinese companies to bid for overseas assets, but will the extra pricing power be enough to overcome political hurdles to cross-border mergers and acquisitions? Headlines In The Past Hour India Trade Min:Yuan Revaluation A Step Toward Mkt Econ Other Market Stories: =China Revaluation Dents Japan Stocks; No Steep Fall Seen =INTERVIEW: China Yuan Impact On Treasurys Limited - CIBC Euro/Yuan At 9.9641 At 0330 GMT Fri Vs 10.0641 Thu US Dollar Down At MYR3.7900 After MYR Unpegging Hong Kong Dollar/Yuan Opens At 1.0638 Vs 1.0638 Thu Yen Opens At CNY7.3000 Per 100 Yen Vs 7.3664 Thu China Sets JPY/CNY Ctrl Pt 7.3327 Per Y100; 7.3664 Thu China Sets EUR/CNY Ctrl Pt 9.8609 Vs 10.0641 Thu Close Shanghai Index +0.7% At 1028.14 At 0142 GMT On CNY Move USD/SGD At 1.6578 Vs 1.6565 As MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  -Dealers =Australian Dollar Rallies After \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  Moves On Yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  Govt Bonds On Bourse Open Mostly Dn After Revalue =FOCUS: Yuan Revaluation Seen Too Small To Impact Metals Canada Afternoon: C$ Higher After Chinese Revaluation US Swaps: Spreads Widen As Tsys Fall On China Revaluation Yuan Revaluation Short Term Negative For Mortgage Bonds Chinese Companies' ADRs Move Up On Yuan Revaluation China \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Revaluation To Boost HK, China-Related Shrs China Yuan Revaluation Likely To Help Chinese Stocks, Bonds India Rupee May Add To Gains After Yuan Revaluation Malaysia Econ, Markets May Gain From Unpegged Ringgit Stronger Yuan A Blow To Argentina's Weak Peso Policy Reaction Stories From Around The World American Malaysian Chamber Of Commerce Backs MYR Move Greenspan: China \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Move `Is A Good First Step' Japan Takenaka:Yuan Move Desirable For China,Global Econ METI Nakagawa: China Yuan Move Mixed Impact On Japan Econ Japan Bank Min Ito: China Move 1st Step Toward \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Reform Korea Fin Min:To Monitor \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Mkt, To Fully Respond-Report Tsy's Snow: China Move "Important Step" For World Economy UK Brown: China Yuan Revaluation To Aid Stability, Growth FOCUS: Euro Policy-Makers, Cos Hail China \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Move IMF: China Should Use Full Scope Of \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Flexibility BOJ: Highly Appreciate China's Decision On Yuan Japan MOF Watanabe Welcomes Chinese Yuan Revaluation Japan Tanigaki: Welcome China's Decision On Yuan-Kyodo Yuan Move A Plus For Brazil, But Little Immediate Impact OECD: China's Yuan Move To Support Rapid Growth Singapore MAS: Yuan Revualation Won't Have Major Impact Thai Ctrl Banker: Yuan Change Good For China, World, Baht Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : No Change To \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Policy Philippine Ctrl Bk Expects Peso Gain On Yuan Revaluation China's \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Move Seen Benefiting Argentina's Farmers US Tsy Official: No Big Impact On Tsy Mkt From China Move Commentary: =\b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Focus: Dlr Outlook Little Changed After Yuan Move  \par \par \uc2 As the dollar recovers at least some of the losses it sustained after China's yuan revaluation, it is becoming increasingly clear that not very much has changed. =ASIA ECONOMY WATCH: China, Asian Econs Likely Resilient  \par \par \uc2 China's move is unlikely to dent significantly the country's strong economic growth, which means that Asian economies also are likely to remain resilient, analysts say. The impact depends on whether Thursday's move is followed by further revaluations, and economists are divided as to the likelihood and timing of more adjustments. =ASIA DEBT: Stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  To Mean Bond Gains Going Forward  \par \par \uc2 Asian local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds fell early Friday in a kneejerk response to China's surprise revaluation of the yuan, but recovered quickly in anticipation that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation in the region will stave off interest rate hikes. Stronger Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are also ultimately likely to help those countries - like the Philippines, Indonesia, Thailand and China - which have local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revenues and large U.S. dollar-denominated liabilities. =POINT OF VIEW: China's Yuan Move To Help Its M&A In U.S.  \par \par \uc2 China's modest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revaluation might have an outsized impact on Chinese companies' ability to execute takeovers in the U.S. The move might weaken U.S. Congressional and other opposition enough to allow future Chinese company attempts to buy U.S. counterparts to attain a greater degree of economic normalcy. =\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  VIEW: China's \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Reform Begins To Crawl  \par \par \uc2 Reform of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system picked up speed Thursday - it's now moving at a crawl.  \par \par \uc2 That won't be fast enough a pace to satisfy the harshest U.S. critics of Chinese policy, but it will probably win the Chinese government more time in which to take bigger and stronger strides towards \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility. =BIG PICTURE: China's Yuan Move No Panacea For Deficit  \par \par \uc2 Chairman Mao is credited with saying the longest journey begins with the first step. On Thursday, the People's Bank of China took the first step on a very long journey when it announced an adjustment to the yuan's exchange rate value. =\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  VIEW: China Move Hits \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market Where It Hurts  \par \par \uc2 For many \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators and investors, China's revaluation of the yuan added a painful punctuation to what has been a problematic time.  \par \par \uc2 -0-  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050722e17m0066b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
