\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Special Summary: China, Malaysia Abandon  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Pegs  \b0\par\par\uc2 1,635 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2005\par 05:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 China and Malaysia have ended their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pegs and will allow a managed float against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones Newswires' coverage can be found by searching on the code M/CNY and M/MYR. Here is a summary of the main stories about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -peg changes. China Abandons \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Peg, Revalues Yuan 2% Higher  \par \par \uc2 In a long-awaited move, China abandoned its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg Thursday and said it would allow the yuan to trade against a basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a so-called managed float regime. China: Non-USD CNY Pairs To Have 1.5% Limit On Each Side  \par \par \uc2 China on Friday announced a daily trading limit of 1.5% on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  other than the U.S. dollar that are traded against the yuan. The range is wider than the 0.3% daily trading limit China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set for the main dollar-yuan pair, announced late Thursday. The limits take effect immediately. Malaysia Severs Ringgit's Link To US \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 In lockstep with China, Malaysia announced that it was abandoning its almost seven-year-old \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to the dollar in favor of a managed float, a move some bankers and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  specialists suggest could provide the domestic economy with at least a short-term boost. Japan Tanigaki: China Revaluation 'A Starting Point'  \par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki on Friday said China's move to revalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a 'starting point' on the way to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform.  \par \par \uc2 'CNY 8.11 (to the dollar) is merely a result of initial action,' Tanigaki told reporters at a regular press conference. 'I think the yuan rate will move according to the basket system,' he said. Japan Hosoda: Don't See Impact On Japan Econ Of Yuan Move  \par \par \uc2 Japan's top government spokesman said Friday that China's revaluation of the yuan is unlikely to have a big impact on Japan's economy.  \par \par \uc2 Chief Cabinet Secretary Hiroyuki Hosoda praised Beijing's steps to make the yuan more flexible, but said that he would also welcome further yuan-policy reform. S Korea Fin Min: Yuan Won't Affect USD/KRW Much - Report  \par \par \uc2 South Korea's Minister of Finance and Economy Han Duck-Soo said Friday the stronger yuan won't affect the Korean won against the U.S. dollar much, and reiterated the government will act if there is volatility in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, according to online news provider edaily. Australia Acting PM: China \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Move Good For Exports  \par \par \uc2 Mark Vaile, Australia's acting prime minister and trade minister, said that China's decision to revalue the yuan is a plus for Australian exports and international markets.  \par \par \uc2 'China is Australia's second largest export market and the revaluation of the renminbi will make Australian exports cheaper, having a positive impact especially on resources and agriculture products,' Vaile said in a statement. The Markets: USD/CNY Opens At 8.11 After China's Revaluation  \par \par \uc2 The dollar began trading at CNY8.11 Friday, according to the China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trading System. By 0145 GMT, the dollar had risen to CNY8.1105, the CFETS showed. Malaysia KLCI Opens Up 1.8% After Ringgit Unpegging  \par \par \uc2 Malaysian shares opened higher Friday, with the weighted Composite Index of 100 blue-chip stocks up 1.8%, or 16.16 points, to 938.10 in early trading. US Dollar Down At MYR3.7900 After MYR Unpegging  \par \par \uc2 The Malaysian ringgit strengthened by 0.3% against the U.S. dollar Friday. The U.S. dollar was trading at 3.7900 against the ringgit in early trading, slightly weaker than the MYR3.80 level it was pegged at since 1998. Treasurys Endure Torrid Session After China Revalues  \par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasurys suffered a torrid bout of selling after China finally enacted a long-awaited revaluation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan, and Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan completed his second day of bullish testimony on the economy before Congress. World \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Falls, Yen Spikes On Yuan Revaluation  \par \par \uc2 The yen and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  spiked against the dollar and the euro Thursday, as China surprised \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by revaluing its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Headlines In The Past Hour China Sets JPY/CNY Ctrl Pt 7.3327 Per Y100; 7.3664 Thu China Sets EUR/CNY Ctrl Pt 9.8609 Vs 10.0641 Thu Close S&P:China's Yuan Move Should Lead To Further Econ Reform China's Yuan Move Unlikely To Hurt Japan Refiners Exports Other Market Stories: US Dollar Down At MYR3.7900 After MYR Unpegging Hong Kong Dollar/Yuan Opens At 1.0638 Vs 1.0638 Thu Yen Opens At CNY7.3000 Per 100 Yen Vs 7.3664 Thu Shanghai Index +0.7% At 1028.14 At 0142 GMT On CNY Move USD/SGD At 1.6578 Vs 1.6565 As MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  -Dealers =Australian Dollar Rallies After \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  Moves On Yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  Govt Bonds On Bourse Open Mostly Dn After Revalue =FOCUS: Yuan Revaluation Seen Too Small To Impact Metals Canada Afternoon: C$ Higher After Chinese Revaluation US Swaps: Spreads Widen As Tsys Fall On China Revaluation Yuan Revaluation Short Term Negative For Mortgage Bonds Chinese Companies' ADRs Move Up On Yuan Revaluation China \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Revaluation To Boost HK, China-Related Shrs China Yuan Revaluation Likely To Help Chinese Stocks, Bonds India Rupee May Add To Gains After Yuan Revaluation Malaysia Econ, Markets May Gain From Unpegged Ringgit Stronger Yuan A Blow To Argentina's Weak Peso Policy Reaction Stories From Around The World Greenspan: China \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Move `Is A Good First Step' Japan Takenaka:Yuan Move Desirable For China,Global Econ METI Nakagawa: China Yuan Move Mixed Impact On Japan Econ Japan Bank Min Ito: China Move 1st Step Toward \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Reform Korea Fin Min:To Monitor \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Mkt, To Fully Respond-Report World Governments, Central Banks Hail China Revaluation US Officials Welcome Yuan Revaluation As Good First Step US Tsy Snow Welcomes China's \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Move Tsy's Snow: China Move 'Important Step' For World Economy ECB Trichet: Chinese Yuan Decision Is Welcome G7 Fin Mins Welcome China Yuan Move UK Brown: China Yuan Revaluation To Aid Stability, Growth FOCUS: Euro Policy-Makers, Cos Hail China \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Move IMF: China Should Use Full Scope Of \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Flexibility BOJ: Highly Appreciate China's Decision On Yuan Japan MOF Watanabe Welcomes Chinese Yuan Revaluation Japan Tanigaki: Welcome China's Decision On Yuan-Kyodo German BGA: China's Yuan Revaluation Only A First Step  \par \par \uc2 -German BGA Group: Further Yuan Revaluation Steps Needed Germany's Eichel Welcomes China's Yuan Revaluation French Fin Min: Yuan Revaluation In Line With G7 Wishes Yuan Move A Plus For Brazil, But Little Immediate Impact OECD: China's Yuan Move To Support Rapid Growth Singapore MAS: Yuan Revualation Won't Have Major Impact Thai Ctrl Banker: Yuan Change Good For China, World, Baht Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : No Change To \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Policy Philippine Ctrl Bk Expects Peso Gain On Yuan Revaluation China's \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Move Seen Benefiting Argentina's Farmers US Tsy Official: No Big Impact On Tsy Mkt From China Move Other Stories: Full Text Of China \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Statement On Yuan Change RATINGS WATCH: China Upgrade Factored In Revaluation China PBOC: Raises Upper Limit For USD, HKD Deposit Rates =UPDATE: Hong Kong Still Satisified With Peg System US Stks Outlook: China's Yuan Move Offers Opportunities US Cos Likely To Remain Indebted To China Despite Reval China's Float Of Yuan Could Increase Tech Part Costs WSJ: US Specialist On China Sees Good And Bad In Yuan Move BIS: Yuan Move A Welcome Step Towards \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Flexibility US Sen Graham: China Move Achieves Much Of What Was Sought US Sens Schumer,Graham Suspend Vote On China Tariff Bill US Sen: China \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Move A 'Good 1st Step...Baby Step' Sen Grassley: China \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Move 'By No Means End Of The Road' US Cos May Seen Higher Funding Costs On China Yuan Move Retailers Still Have Options After China's \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Move China \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Float May Level M&A Playing Field In US Commentary: =POINT OF VIEW: China's Yuan Move To Help Its M&A In U.S.  \par \par \uc2 China's modest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revaluation might have an outsized impact on Chinese companies' ability to execute takeovers in the U.S. The move might weaken U.S. Congressional and other opposition enough to allow future Chinese company attempts to buy U.S. counterparts to attain a greater degree of economic normalcy. =\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  VIEW: China's \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Reform Begins To Crawl  \par \par \uc2 Reform of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system picked up speed Thursday - it's now moving at a crawl.  \par \par \uc2 That won't be fast enough a pace to satisfy the harshest U.S. critics of Chinese policy, but it will probably win the Chinese government more time in which to take bigger and stronger strides towards \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility. =BIG PICTURE: China's Yuan Move No Panacea For Deficit  \par \par \uc2 Chairman Mao is credited with saying the longest journey begins with the first step. On Thursday, the People's Bank of China took the first step on a very long journey when it announced an adjustment to the yuan's exchange rate value. =\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  VIEW: China Move Hits \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market Where It Hurts  \par \par \uc2 For many \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators and investors, China's revaluation of the yuan added a painful punctuation to what has been a problematic time. Other Commentary: =GLOBAL YIELD: It's Small, But China Move Packs Punch =ECB Watch:China Yuan Move Makes ECB Rate Cut Less Likely =AWSJ: Yuan Revaluation Gives China Monetary Flexibility =AWSJ: China Yuan Move May Spur Pressure For More Change =\b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Focus: Speculation On Yuan Will Increase Now =FOCUS: Yuan Move Has Limited Impact On Oil Markets =CHARTING AMERICAS: Dollar Continues Its Own Revaluation =\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  VIEW: Chinese Revaluation Short-Term Boost For C$  \par \par \uc2 -0-  \p