\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Yen surges after China abandons dollar  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  peg  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natsuko Waki and Katie Hunt  \par \uc2 803 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 2005\par 14:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates price moves, adds official reaction)  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, July 21 (Reuters) - The yen rose 2 percent versus the dollar and rallied against the euro on Thursday after China abandoned its dollar peg in favour of a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to manage the yuan, allowing it to appreciate to 8.11 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The yen's gains, which also came after Malaysia changed the ringgit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to a managed float, triggered a chain reaction in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar surged 2 percent before dealers reported the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth its appreciation.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's long-awaited revaluation from the previous 8.28 per dollar was smaller than many economists had expected. But it nevertheless sent a shockwave through the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as investors were losing patience with their unprofitable bets on the yen -- used as a proxy for yuan revaluation speculation.  \par \par \uc2 "It was going to happen at some point. They have introduced a very modest appreciation to kick the whole thing off," said Ian Gunner, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Mellon Financial Corporation.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is now going to be interested in how much further there is to go. There could be another adjustment in a few months but I do not think they will want to get into a timetable here."  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has risen to a three-week high of 110.18 per dollar, a whole 2 yen gain from pre-announcement levels around 112.40.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was on track for its biggest daily gains since March 2002 on percentage terms. However, by 1445 GMT it had trimmed gains to 110.78.  \par \par \uc2 The yen also rose to 134.26 per euro from around 136.60 before the announcement, around 1 percent higher from late New York levels. Within 30 minutes of the yuan news the yen rose 1.2 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's reaction was muted against the euro. It fell initially to the day's low of $1.2255 per euro from around $1.2140 but reversed losses to stand at $1.2115, up a quarter percent on the day.  \par \par \uc2 State-run Xinhua news agency said China would continue to manage the yuan in a range of plus/minus 0.3 percent against the dollar and would aim to keep the yuan basically stable at a balanced and rational level.  \par \par \uc2 MORE TO COME?  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar, widely used with the yen to bet on a yuan move, shot higher to a two-month high of 1.6503 per U.S. dollar, up 2 percent on the day compared with 1.6843 on Wednesday, before dealers reported the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Singapore said it will maintain its policy of gradual and modest strengthening of the Singapre dollar and said fundamentals of the city-state's economy had not changed.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong said it would not consider changing its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to the dollar even if the yuan keep appreciating and said the Hong Kong dollar will remain very stable.  \par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee rose to a six-year peak against the dollar around 43.20, up more than half a percent.  \par \par \uc2 "The move is clearly positive for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  first, and to some extent the euro. It is pretty clear that the basket will involve a reasonable chunk of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Emanuele Ravano, European strategist at PIMCO in London.  \par \par \uc2 The Korean won's non-deliverable forward prices, used by offshore investors to trade the won, showed investors are factoring in a 2.2 percent rise in the won/dollar rate in one-month's time.  \par \par \uc2 The won closed at 1,035.5 per dollar in the local market.  \par \par \uc2 "It's still difficult to interpret. We don't know vital elements like the weights of the different \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the basket -- indeed if we ever get to know that," said Adam Cole, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Royal Bank of Canada.  \par \par \uc2 Politicians worldwide welcomed China's move although the 2.1 percent revaluation to 8.11 per dollar stopped short of what many of China's trading partners had hoped for.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow welcomed China's move to let its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade more freely and noted that the United States expects more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves from Beijing.  \par \par \uc2 Following the yen's rise of more than two percent, Japan's top financial diplomat Hiroshi Watanabe said he is watching the market carefully and would take action if needed.  \par \par \uc2 Japan has been urging China to reform the rigid \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime but it had repeatedly said the yuan revaluation doesn't mean a higher yen and it has hinted it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-YEN-YUAN (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050721e17l001yr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
