\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Bank Of Canada Dodge:China Should Move Soon To  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Float-2  \b0\par\par\uc2 660 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2005\par 05:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 'We think China should move as quickly as possible to a floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' Dodge said.  \par \par \uc2 'We are not arguing that they should revalue, because a modest revaluation is not in China's or the world economy's interests,' he said.  \par \par \uc2 Dodge also reiterated the Bank of Canada's long-standing view that floating exchange rates best allow an economy to adjust to external shocks.  \par \par \uc2 Dodge said that when an economy has a fixed exchange rate, wages and prices can't respond flexibly to changes in the global economy, leading to shrinking output, rising unemployment or very high inflation.  \par \par \uc2 Financial authorities have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to keep an exchange rate fixed. If this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is 'sterilized,' as is the case in \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , then this also temporarily prevents movements in wages and prices, Dodge said.  \par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sterilizes \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by issuing short-term debt instruments to soak up the liquidity it added to the money supply through its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 In the past, Japan has also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to prevent the yen from appreciating. However, it's unreasonable to compare Japan to \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  because Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 