e U.K. and the U.S. - we haven't generated the levels of inflation that we saw in the 60s, 70s or 80s,' Dodge said.  \par \par \uc2 'Something has been happening to traditional relationships that we don't fully understand,' he said.  \par \par \uc2 Dodge repeated the Bank of Canada's view that interest rates will have to rise 'over time.' The Bank of Canada has left its trend-setting overnight rate unchanged at 2.5% at its last five policy meetings. Its next meeting is July 12.  \par \par \uc2 He also said he expects inflation in Canada to be near its target by the end of 2006. Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  currently aims to keep on-year rises in the core consumer price index at the midpoint of a 1.0% to 3.0% target band. This inflation target is up for review in 2006. -By Stanley White, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; stanley.white@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Hugh Lawson and Shawn Schroter  \par \par \uc2 -0-  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050609e1690020b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
