\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-China yuan move still a puzzle for  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2  traders.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Jamie McGeever  \par \uc2 815 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 April 2005\par 20:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, April 29 (Reuters) - Speculation that China could soon allow its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade more freely is reaching fever pitch, but the road to a stronger yuan is still dotted with speed bumps that are making investors cautious with their bets.  \par \par \uc2 "The Chinese have shown themselves quite capable of digging deep into the trenches and not being terribly responsive to outside needs," agreed Alan Ruskin, director at 4Cast, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fixed income research firm in New York.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan, or renminbi, is pegged in a narrow band around 8.28 per dollar. As the dollar has broadly weakened over the last three and a half years, so the falling yuan has made Chinese goods cheaper on export markets.  \par \par \uc2 Faced with a global flood of those Chinese goods, especially textiles and clothing, the United States and European nations have been saying China must revalue.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow reiterated his demand for a more flexible Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the Group of Seven meetings in Washington, saying financial conditions in China were in place for a change of yuan policy.  \par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan added his voice to the chorus, saying it was in China's interest to loosen the exchange rate "sooner rather than later."  \par \par \uc2 The message from Chinese officials isn't consistent.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Zhou Xiaochun told Reuters last week that there are no serious political or technical obstacles to revaluing the yuan. But Wei Benhua, the deputy chief of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulator, said he was not in favor of a revaluation this year or early next.  \par \par \uc2 Amid this uncertainty over timing, derivatives trading in the yen - one proxy for the yuan - suggests dealers are still cautious about betting on a yuan revaluation.  \par \par \uc2 Implied volatility on euro/yen options, a measure of anticipated swings in the pair's exchange rate over a given period of time, remain at historically low levels despite their spike to a three-month high Friday.  \par \par \uc2 "I think the market's getting ahead of itself," said the senior dealer at a Japanese bank in New York. "This could be short-lived."  \par \par \uc2 China's trading partners, meanwhile, are considering measures of their own to stem the flow.  \par \par \uc2 A U.S. senator has proposed a bill slapping 27.5 percent tariffs on all Chinese imports, while both the Washington and the EU are considering industry demands to consider action to restrain imports of some Chinese goods.  \par \par \uc2 But such legislation from rich countries could backfire, riling Beijing and delaying any freeing up of the yuan.  \par \par \uc2 "China will see that as a very provocative action," said Paresh Upadhyaya, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Putnam Investments in Boston.  \par \par \uc2 Similarly, Beijing would also bristle if the U.S. Treasury names China explicitly in its periodic report on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market manipulation due for release in the coming weeks.  \par \par \uc2 That would also draw "an immediate and strongly worded response" from Chinese officials, followed by silence and an assumption a yuan move would be pushed back, Upadhyaya said.  \par \par \uc2 NOT A SLAM DUNK  \par \par \uc2 European sources at the G7 meeting said the United States had sought a specific mention of China in the communique but that other G7 members resisted singling out China.  \par \par \uc2 Recent comments from Chinese officials suggest they are ready to do something, such as widen the yuan's trading band.  \par \par \uc2 But Stephen Jen, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Morgan Stanley in London, suggests that by signalling a willingness to bow to international pressure, Chinese officials may actually be actually buying more time.  \par \par \uc2 A rising yuan would likely put upward pressure on other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as monetary authorities in the region would be more tolerant of strength in their local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in exchange for China being prepared to lose some of its competitive advantage.  \par \par \uc2 The uncertainty over timing means that, from a trading perspective, proxy trades for a yuan revaluation such as selling the euro against the Japanese yen aren't cheap, risk-free positions either.  \par \par \uc2 "Everyone agrees it's coming but it's a timing thing. You can't just sit on your position because that costs you money," said Scott Ainsbury, portfolio manager at \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Concepts, a $12 billion hedge fund in New York.  \par \par \uc2 Holding Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in anticipation of a yuan revaluation "is a trade you have to have on...but a lot of people already have it on."  \par \par \uc2 It cannot be assumed that a widening of the yuan's trading band will see trade and investment flows into China immediately strengthen the yuan anyway, analysts said, because pent-up Chinese demand to invest abroad is also thought to be high.  \par \par \uc2 Looking further ahead, speculative inflows into China may be so huge as to force the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to actually increase dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability, analysts at UBS said.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050429e14t00hwl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
