\par\par \b \uc2 US Tsy's Taylor: China Should Move Now To Flexible  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 2005\par 19:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--China should move now toward a more flexible exchange rate system, the U.S. Treasury's top international policymaker said Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "We have very much stressed they can begin to have a flexible exchange rate right now," U.S. Treasury Undersecretary for International Affairs John Taylor told reporters in a briefing ahead of the joint International Monetary Fund and World Bank spring meetings.  \par \par \uc2 China has come under increasing pressure from the U.S., Europe, and the IMF to ease its tightly managed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to the U.S. dollar. The Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, purchasing dollars to prevent the yuan from appreciating. Earlier Thursday, the Chinese government reported its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves jumped $49.2 billion in the first quarter to a record $659.1 billion, a symptom of that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The IMF has urged \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to adopt more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility, so that monetary policy can focus more on fighting inflation in the rapidly growing economy. The Fund has also argued that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation in Asia is a key to alleviating massive global trade imbalances.  \par \par \uc2 Taylor noted that China has taken a number of steps to prepare for a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , for example discussing the establishment of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedging instruments with the Chicago Mercantile Exchange.  \par \par \uc2 "Now is the time, given those steps were taken to move ahead," he said.  \par \par \uc2 On Argentina's debt restructuring, shaping up to be a topic for a G7 finance ministers' meeting on Saturday, Taylor said the high participation rate in the government's debt restructuring offer is a "good sign."  \par \par \uc2 It is important for Argentina's government to continue to talk with creditors who rejected the offer, he added.  \par \par \uc2 -By Elizabeth Price, Dow Jones Newswires; 202-862-9295; Elizabeth.Price@dowjones.com [ 14-04-05 1730GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050414e14e000se\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
