\par\par \b \uc2 TEXT-S.Korea plays down Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  impact of any yuan reform.  \b0\par\par\uc2 400 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 07:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, March 17 (Reuters) - South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday a potential revaluation of China's yuan against the U.S. dollar was unlikely to push other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  sharply higher against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of Korea said in a report summarising international economic\par affairs that the won             and the Taiwan dollar          had\par made strong gains against the U.S. dollar and were unlikely to gain\par much more even if the yuan was revalued.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Following are some key summaries from the report, translated by Reuters:  \par \par \uc2 TALK OF ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  APPRECIATING WHEN YUAN REGIME CHANGES:  \par \par \uc2 "As expectations for the yuan's revaluation eased after the Group of Seven meeting from Feb. 4-5, and as the yuan's appreciation eased in non-deliverable forward trading, most experts have forecast that China would first try to increase flexibility in its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  system.  \par \par \uc2 "But Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened on expectations that the yuan will appreciate once the flexibility in China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  system is heightened."  \par \par \uc2 BUT POSSIBILITY SEEN LOW FOR ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  TO APPRECIATE EVEN WHEN FLEXIBILITY IN THE YUAN SYSTEM RAISED:  \par \par \uc2 "Even if the flexibility of the yuan is heightened, the scope of its appreciation is very likely to be limited within tolerable ranges due to possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Even if the yuan appreciates following the increased flexibility in the yuan system, it will not have a big impact on improving the trade balances (with) Asian countries and therefore will not likely play a role in sparking a follow-up appreciation of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in these countries.  \par \par \uc2 "In fact, the co-relation between the yuan and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very low in non-deliverable forward trading, which reflects market expectations.  \par \par \uc2 "On the other hand, the possibility is relatively low that the South Korean won and the Taiwan dollar, which have already appreciated considerably, will face additional appreciation pressure.  \par \par \uc2 "As for the Indian government, it is expected to be reluctant to tolerate an appreciation of the rupee because it has said further appreciation of the rupee was not desirable amid a current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 "Moreover, the scope of appreciation in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely be limited because each country is expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market when the appreciation pressure builds up on yen and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the yuan's appreciation."   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050317e13h005va\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
