\par\par \b \uc2 Daily Chinese yuan update.  \b0\par\par\uc2 424 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 09:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, March 1 (Reuters) - Following is a summary of market activity and news articles relating to the Chinese yuan on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  *** The yuan  ended a notch stronger at 8.2764 per\par  U.S. dollar, near the stronger end of its managed trading range.\par  *** The one-year non-deliverable dollar forward discount\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 versus the yuan was at 3,450 points, implying a rate of 7.933 yuan per dollar in 12 months' time.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NDFs are a transaction where a forward price is agreed between a customer and a bank, but settlement on the value date is undertaken entirely in U.S. dollars.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *** One-year implied yuan volatility was traded at 5.70/6.85 percent.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Implied volatility is a measure of how much the options market expects the price of the underlying asset to move during the life of the option.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan moves in a band of 8.2760 to 8.2800 enforced by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turnover, a moderate $970 million on Monday, was not immediately available. The yuan softened to 7.9239 against 100 Japanese yen from 7.9108 on Monday, but it ended stronger against the euro at 10.9067 from 10.9759.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OPEN MARKET ACTIVITY  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold 60 billion yuan in short-term bills on Tuesday, versus a modest 35 billion yuan last week, and siphoned off another 5 billion yuan by entering into repurchase agreements.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEWS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China to let global agencies sell maiden yuan bonds  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING/SHANGHAI - China unveiled rules on Tuesday that will let international development agencies issue yuan-denominated bonds for the first time, hoping to deepen the country's fledgling bond market and expand investors' options.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - ~- --  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China parliament to help slow economy, assist poor  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING - China's economic bosses will reinforce measures to slow the country's racing economic growth at the annual parliamentary session this month while trying to ensure hundreds of millions of poor farmers are not left behind.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - ~- --  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 2004 hit $195 bln  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SHANGHAI - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Tuesday it spent 1.61 trillion yuan ($195 billion) buying foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 2004 to maintain the yuan peg against the dollar, a rise of 40 percent over 2003.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - ~- --  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China warns against relaxing macro controls-paper  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING - China's development chief, Ma Kai, has warned against being too optimistic after initial successes in cooling fixed asset investment growth and urged macro-economic controls to be kept in place, the People's Daily said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - ~- --.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050301e1310079b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
