\par\par \b \uc2 PRESS DIGEST-Asian Wall Street Journal - Feb. 22.  \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2005\par 00:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Feb 22 (Reuters) - The following stories were reported in Tuesday's electronic version of The Asian Wall Street Journal:  \par \par \uc2 * Toyota Motor (7203.T) will likely add two more assembly plants in North America by the end of the decade as part of its strategy to take a bigger market share and challenge GM (GM.N) as the world's No. 1 auto maker.  \par \par \uc2 * Nissan's (7201.T) chief will hand day-to-day management to Toshiyuki Shiga on Apr. 1, when the auto maker's CEO, Carlos Ghosn, adds the post of Renault's chief executive.  \par \par \uc2 * CAO Singapore's (CNAO.SI) Chinese parent denied allegations by the unit's suspended CEO that Beijing executives could have cut the unit's derivatives losses if they had acted more quickly.  \par \par \uc2 * A Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said easing some lending controls could help promote non-bank lending, providing funding for small and midsize firms and individual borrowers.  \par \par \uc2 * Japanese officials have been warning that Tokyo is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yen rises on a \b \highlight22\uc2 China currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -policy change.  \par \par \uc2 * Chinese regulators announced a protection fund for securities investors in China, but analysts awaited more details and said it is unlikely to address key investor concerns.  \par \par \uc2 * Fairfax (FXJ.AX) reported net profit for its first half fell 18 percent due to year-earlier one-time gains. The Australian publisher's chief executive signalled its potential interest in acquiring one of the country's major TV networks.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Sovereign said the Monaco-based fund supports the managements of\par Korea's LG Corp.  and LG Electronics            , in which it has taken\par 6% stakes, and doesn't intend to replace them.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * AXA Asia Pacific (AXA.AX) said profit fell 42 percent, reflecting a year-earlier gain, and the unit of France's AXA said it is looking at India's funds and life-insurance market.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Spot prices of DRAM chips continue to fall as Chinese demand for personal computers slows, and dealers say it is difficult to predict when the market might turn around.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050221e12l00njb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
