\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won, peso rise as G7 dominates.  \b0\par\par\uc2 945 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2005\par 09:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 27 (Reuters) - The Korean won jumped to a\par seven-year high and the Philippine peso rose to its highest in\par a year on Thursday, as rising rhetoric ahead of next week's\par Group of Seven nations' meeting boosted the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The won stalled around 1,027 a dollar, a November 1997\par peak, and the Sing dollar bounced off levels close to 1.63 per\par dollar as regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reacted to fluctuations in the\par offshore Chinese yuan forwards and statements ahead of the Feb.\par 4 and 5 G7 meeting.\par     China has been invited to talks with the G7.\par     Simon Flint, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with Bank of America, said\par the volatility would persist until next week.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "You will get rhetoric from G7 stressing the burden-sharing\par and the need for flexibility in places there isn't any,\par particularly China, and you will have some impact on\par non-Japanese Asia as well," he said, referring to the growing\par calls from the United States and Europe for Asia to help\par correct global imbalances arising from the huge U.S. trade\par deficit.\par     "But you will continue to hear comments from the Chinese\par officials trying to dampen down expectations of how soon they\par will make any change," he said.\par  \par     "You would expect the rhetoric to create some choppiness in\par markets."\par     The regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  found support in U.S. President\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 George W. Bush's comment on Wednesday that countries should let  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 market forces determine the value of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and that  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the United States was working with China on the issue.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governing council member Nout Wellink  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said Asian central banks could not keep buying dollars forever,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 referring to Asia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to hold back \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, news that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief Zhou  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Xiaochuan will attend talks with the G7 officials when they  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 meet in London on Feb. 4 and 5 propped up yuan offshore  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 premiums  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese yuan non-deliverable forwards - derivatives used  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to speculate on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - showed one-year premiums on the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 yuan moving between 4,100 and 3,950 points, pricing in an  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 appreciation of between 5.2 and 5.0 percent.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KOREAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said the won rose partly as the Korean authorities  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 had difficulty \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to rein it in. Rising yields in the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 local debt market restrained them from issuing more bonds to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 offset the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "They are struggling with the back-up in interest rates.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 They are absolutely hamstrung in terms of being able to  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in any big way," one analyst said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "The only saviour is that it is very difficult for the\par market to sell dollar/won when yen/won is below 10."\par     The rising won has caused the yen-won cross rate to fall to\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 its lowest levels since August 2003. The cross hit 9.87 won per  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 yen on Tuesday and stayed below the sensitive 10 level on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wednesday and Thursday.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analysts believe Korean authorities, keenly  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 conscious of the won's competitiveness in export markets versus  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the yen, prefer to see the cross rate stay above 10 won per  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 yen.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 And that posed a dilemma for markets, on whether to sell  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the won expecting it to slide versus the yen or to buy won on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the belief the Koreans could not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PESO STRENGTH  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, the Philippine peso extended its newfound  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 strength to hit 55.13 per dollar, its strongest since January  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2004.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said the peso furthered its rally after lead  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 managers for a Philippine 25-year sovereign bond issue managed  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to sell $1.5 billion, against a targeted $1 billion, and at a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 lower yield than initially indicated.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The passage of a bill by the lower house of Congress to\par raise the value-added tax also bolstered sentiment.\par     "Nothing fundamental has changed but sentiment has\par definitely shifted," said James Malcolm, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist\par with Deutsche Bank.\par     A host of factors helped change sentiment, Malcolm said,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 including falling Indonesian yields and the rupiah's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 sluggishness which had led markets to search for an alternate  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 high-yielding asset.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders also attributed the peso rally to the inflow of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 around $156 million to fund Japan's Kirin Brewery Co. Ltd's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 purchase of a stake in San Miguel Corp., which pushed the peso  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 higher earlier this month because the Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 did not absorb the entire amount.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "More broadly, nothing much has happened in the Philippines  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for a while despite all the negative publicity. And, in an  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 environment where nothing much was happening, people were  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 getting more focused on yield plays, some people are beginning  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to say the Philippines looks good fundamentally because tax  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 reforms are going through," Malcolm said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0825 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.06         103.56       +0.49\par  Sing dlr        1.6323         1.6367       +0.27\par  Taiwan dlr      31.863         31.894       +0.10\par  Korean won     1028.00        1031.50       +0.34\p