\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -G7 rhetoric dominates - won, peso up.  \b0\par\par\uc2 837 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2005\par 04:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 27 (Reuters) - The Korean won jumped to a\par seven-year high and the Philippine peso rose to its highest in\par a year on Thursday as rising rhetoric ahead of next week's\par Group of Seven nations' meeting boosted the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were bolstered by U.S. President George W.\par Bush's comment on Wednesday that countries should let market\par forces determine the value of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and that the\par United States was working with China on the issue.\par     European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governing council member Nout Wellink\par said Asian central banks could not keep buying dollars forever,\par referring to Asia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to hold back \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Meanwhile, news that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief Zhou\par Xiaochuan will attend talks with the G7 officials when they\par meet in London on Feb.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  4 and 5 propped up yuan offshore\par premiums     "The talk of greater exchange rate flexibility\par will continue to dominate headlines going through the G7\par meeting next week," ING said in a note.\par  \par     The Korean won outperformed the region, scaling 1,030 a\par dollar for the first time since November 1997.\par     The Singapore dollar flirted with levels close to 1.63 per\par dollar in early deals but settled around 1.6340 subsequently.\par     The Indonesian rupiah hit a 10-day peak of 9,120 a dollar.\par     KOREAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     Traders said the won rose partly as the Korean authorities\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 had difficulty \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to rein it in. Rising yields in the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 local debt market restrained them from issuing more bonds to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 offset the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "They are struggling with the back-up in interest rates.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 They are absolutely hamstrung in terms of being able to  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in any big way," one analyst said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "The only saviour is that it is very difficult for the\par market to sell dollar/won when yen/won is below 10."\par     The rising won has caused the yen-won cross rate to fall to\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 its lowest levels since August 2003. The cross hit 9.87 won per  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 yen on Tuesday and stayed below the sensitive 10 level on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wednesday and Thursday.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analysts believe Korean authorities, keenly  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 conscious of the won's competitiveness in export markets versus  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the yen, prefer to see the cross rate stay above 10 won per  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 yen.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 And that posed a dilemma for markets, on whether to sell  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the won expecting it to slide versus the yen or to buy won on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the belief the Koreans could not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PESO STRENGTH  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, the Philippine peso extended its newfound  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 strength to hit 55.17 per dollar, its strongest since January  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2004.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said the peso furthered its rally after lead  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 managers for a Philippine 25-year sovereign bond issue managed  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to sell $1.5 billion, against a targeted $1 billion, and at a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 lower yield than initially indicated.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Nothing fundamental has changed but sentiment has  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 definitely shifted," said James Malcolm, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 with Deutsche Bank.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A host of factors helped change sentiment, Malcolm said,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 including falling Indonesian yields and the rupiah's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 sluggishness which had led markets to search for an alternate  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 high-yielding asset.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders also attributed the peso rally to the inflow of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 around $156 million to fund Japan's Kirin Brewery Co. Ltd's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 purchase of a stake in San Miguel Corp., which pushed the peso  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 higher earlier this month because the Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 did not absorb the entire amount.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "More broadly, nothing much has happened in the Philippines  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for a while despite all the negative publicity. And, in an  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 environment where nothing much was happening, people were  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 getting more focused on yield plays, some people are beginning  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to say the Philippines looks good fundamentally because tax  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 reforms are going through," Malcolm said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malcolm said while he expected the peso to drift higher to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 55 a dollar, offshore yields in peso non-deliverable forwards  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 were not high enough. Peso NDFs yielded 5.5 percent for 6  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 months and 6.5 percent for a year, he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Is that good compensation for risk? I am not so sure," he  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day at 0301 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.18         103.56       +0.37\par  Sing dlr        1.6325         1.6367       +0.26\par  Taiwan dlr      31.830         31.894       +0.20\par  Korean won     1027.30        1031.50       +0.41\par  Baht             38.52          38.55       +0.09\par  Peso             55.12          55.33       +0.38\par  Rupiah         9133.00        9140.00       +0.08\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.18         102.45       -0.71\par  Sing dlr        1.6325         1.6310       -0.09\par  Taiwan dlr      31.830         31.917       +0.27\par  Korean won     1027.30        1035.10       +0.76\par  Baht             38.52          38.85       +0.87\par  Peso             55.12          56.28       +2.10\par  Rupiah         9133.00        9270.00       +1.50\par  Rupee            43.79          43.47       -0.72.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050127e11r003ml\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
