\par\par \b \uc2 Daily Chinese yuan update.  \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2005\par 09:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, Jan 6 (Reuters) - Following is a summary of market activity and news articles relating to the Chinese yuan on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  *** The yuan  ended a notch weaker at 8.2765 per\par  U.S. dollar, near the stronger end of its managed trading range.\par  *** The one-year non-deliverable dollar forward discount\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 versus the yuan was at 3,550 points, implying a rate of 7.923 yuan per dollar in 12 months' time.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NDFs are a transaction where a forward price is agreed between a customer and a bank, but settlement on the value date is undertaken entirely in U.S. dollars.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *** One-year implied yuan volatility was at 6.75/8.30 percent.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Implied volatility is a measure of how much the options market expects the price of the underlying asset to move during the life of the option.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan moves in a band of 8.2760 to 8.2800 enforced by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turnover, a strong $1.48 billion on Wednesday, was not immediately available. The yuan strengthened to 7.9033 against 100 Japanese yen from 7.9305 on Wednesday and firmed against the euro to 10.9766 from 11.0026.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OPEN MARKET ACTIVITY  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  drained 23 billion yuan ($2.78 billion) from the banking system on Thursday, up from 15 billion yuan last week, as it strengthened efforts to soak up excess base money.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEWS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  2004 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  put at over $121 bln  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SHANGHAI - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is estimated to have spent substantially more than 1 trillion yuan ($121 billion) to buy hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market in 2004 in order to keep the yuan inside its targeted range, analysts said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full Story:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - ~- --  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remarks may signal reform push  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING - Remarks by China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor that he would "actively and safely" promote \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reform this year may be a fresh sign that Beijing is getting serious about tweaking its long-standing yuan policy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full Story:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - ~- --.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050106e116007q0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
