\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Offshore yuan softer, Sing dollar capped.  \b0\par\par\uc2 824 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2004\par 08:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 22 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surrendered\par their meagre gains on Wednesday after China quashed rumours of\par an imminent yuan policy change and Thailand said it will keep\par the baht competitive for exports.\par     The regionals moved less than a quarter of a percent during\par the day as a lacklustre yen and thinning holiday trade pinned\par the market down. The yen  has marked time in a one yen\par range around 104.25 per dollar since Monday, robbing Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of direction.\par     The Singapore dollar's        moves to the firmer side of\par 1.64 a dollar were short-lived. Fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore, coupled with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's statement\par that it had no plans to revalue the tightly managed yuan before\par the year-end, dragged the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  down.\par  \par     The denial also took the steam out of Chinese yuan\par non-deliverable forwards.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     One-year NDFs were quoted at 4,700 points, down 100 points\par from the day's peak, which had priced in a 6.2 percent\par appreciation in the yuan in a year.\par     "This is a market rumour," a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spokesman said\par when asked about the speculation in offshore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.\par "At present there is no change in the exchange rate policy."\par     The yuan premium had risen this week as traders positioned\par themselves for a possible change in the yuan's virtually fixed\par rate around 8.28 per dollar.\par     "The market was trying to second-guess the Chinese\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 authorities," said Bhanu Baweja of UBS in Singapore. He saw no  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 reason to expect a one-off yuan revaluation or, indeed, any  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 move at all before the end of the year or in early 2005.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "A big revaluation, in terms of market thinking, is driven  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 by political pressure, severe yuan undervaluation and the need  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to slow down the economy by massive revaluation.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I don't think they are going to move for any of these  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 reasons. They will move for a structural reason and that will  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 be a modest move," Baweja said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, the baht stayed in a tight range just a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 shade weaker than 39 per dollar. Bank of Thailand Governor  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pridiyathorn Devakula said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will try to keep  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the baht at a level that is competitive for exporters.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The South Korean won             was also hemmed in a\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 narrow range of 1,053-1,058 per dollar, with little incentive  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to break out after a steep 9 percent rally since October that  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 has made it Asia's top performer so far in 2004.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wariness over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  capped the Taiwan dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 , forcing it to retreat from a 2-week high of 32.22 a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar even as the stock market extended its rally  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 since the start of the month.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Expectations of heavier inflow of dollars from Filipinos  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 working overseas propped up the Philippine peso , despite  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the threat of a sovereign ratings downgrade as lawmakers  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 struggle to rein in a bulging budget deficit.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 INDONESIA INDIFFERENT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian rupiah showed almost no reaction to a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ratings upgrade by Standard & Poor's.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 S&P lifted the country's foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating by a notch  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to B-plus, citing progress in macroeconomic stability and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 fiscal management as well as declining debt and favourable  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 external liquidity.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupiah was steady around 9,325 a dollar, maintaining  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 its weak bias as markets priced in security and political  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 fears.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesian Vice-President Jusuf Kalla's weekend victory in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the contest to lead Golkar, the biggest opposition party, is  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 widely seen as a bonus for President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yet some analysts are concerned Kalla's larger backing  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 could be a threat in the event of disagreements over policy in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's fragmented cabinet.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupiah has also been hurt by security alerts. This  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 week, an old grenade was found in the compound of the Hilton  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 hotel in Jakarta, just days after warnings that militants might  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 attack one of the country's three Hilton hotels.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0730 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.34         104.12       -0.21\par  Sing dlr        1.6404         1.6416       +0.07\par  Taiwan dlr      32.306         32.332       +0.08\par  Korean won     1053.50        1055.40       +0.18\par  Baht             39.04          39.02       -0.05\par  Peso             56.09          56.09       +0.01\par  Rupiah         9320.00        9315.00       -0.05\par  Rupee            43.86          43.79       -0.16\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.34         107.31       +2.85\par  Sing dlr        1.6404         1.6978       +3.50\par  Taiwan dlr      32.306         33.978       +5.18\par  Korean won     1053.50        1192.00      +13.15\par  Baht             39.04          39.59       +1.40\par  Peso             56.09          55.49       -1.06\par  Rupiah         9320.00        8410.00       -9.76\par  Rupee            43.86          45.60       +3.96.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041222e0cm00899\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
