\par\par \b \uc2 China's gripe on dollar seen unlikely to stir G7.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Shinichi Kishima  \par \uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2004\par 09:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 29 (Reuters) - Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao's complaint that too little has been done to halt the dollar's slide and this is preventing Beijing from easing its grip on the yuan could end up being just that - a complaint.  \par \par \uc2 The Group of Seven (G7) economic powers are unlikely to promptly respond with concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given the bickering among themselves and the view that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy is a root cause of global imbalances undermining the dollar, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts said on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 "Given the dollar's downward momentum, it's true China will face a tough battle in the market if they let the yuan move now. It's natural that they want to avoid that," said Taisuke Tanaka, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 "But in terms of coordinated action to stop the dollar's fall, I don't think the G7 will go that far," he added.  \par \par \uc2 Wen, speaking to reporters on Sunday in the Lao capital of Vientiane where he was attending a Southeast Asian summit, said conditions had not been met yet for China to let the yuan, which has been virtually pegged at 8.28 to the dollar, trade more freely on the market.  \par \par \uc2 "We will consider the timing of its implementation. To tell you the truth, the more heated this speculation is, the more these kinds of measures cannot be implemented," Wen said.  \par \par \uc2 He turned the question around, bringing up the dollar's precipitous fall. "Today, we actually have to ask a question. The U.S. dollar is depreciating, with no attempts to manage it. What is the reason for this? Shouldn't the relevant parties take measures?"  \par \par \uc2 BALL IN G7 COURT?  \par \par \uc2 In response to Wen's comments, the offshore non-deliverable forwards (NDF) market showed reduced upward pressure on the yuan. The premium on one-year yuan NDF shrank to about 4,000 points from record highs around 4,500 set late last week.  \par \par \uc2 But the dollar was still seen under pressure, as few traders anticipated any U.S. or G7 action to arrest its fall in the near term.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was barely half a percent above last week's record lows around $1.3330 to the euro and near-five-year lows around 102.15 yen .  \par \par \uc2 Having taken a string of deregulatory steps on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues over the last few weeks, Wen seems to be saying Beijing has done its part for now and the ball is in the G7's court.  \par \par \uc2 But analysts said the market was not being swayed by such political manoeuvres.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is convinced they're just waiting for optimal timing," said Daisuke Uno, a market analystatSumitomo Mitsui Bank.  \par \par \uc2 He added that pushing up the dollar was an unlikely option for the United States when the whole debate has been that the yuan has been undervalued against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 With or without China's prompting, the G7 has had difficulty agreeing on a prescription for a weak dollar.  \par \par \uc2 While Europe and Japan have urged the United States to reduce its gaping current account and budget deficits, Washington has called on its counterparts to boost domestic demand despite the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reluctance to cut interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 "Much like China would not revalue if everyone ganged up on them, it would be counterproductive for China to engage in a war of words," said Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041129e0bt00713\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
