\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-No G20 statement on exchange rates-German source.  \b0\par\par\uc2 419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2004\par 16:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BERLIN, Nov 17 (Reuters) - Finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs from the G20 group of rich and emerging market nations do not plan to issue a statement on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at talks this weekend, a German government source said on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The source said the G20 talks, which kick off with a dinner on Nov. 19 and end at lunchtime on Nov. 21, were not an appropriate forum for exchange rate discussions.  \par \par \uc2 "There won't be any formal discussion on exchange rates ... You should not expect any statement on exchange rates," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar crashed through a record low against the euro and a seven month low versus the yen on Wednesday as markets eyed comments from U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow, travelling in Europe ahead of the G20.  \par \par \uc2 Snow downplayed the effectiveness of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and said it was up to Europe and \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take policy steps to help the U.S. address its yawning trade deficit. European officials reiterated concern over \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility.  \par \par \uc2 Germany, as G20 president, would not put exchange rates on the agenda, the source said. But he did not rule out that some delegations could bring up the issue as part of discussions on the global economic outlook or on the margins of the talks.  \par \par \uc2 "It's clearly difficult to speak intelligently about the world economy without reference to exchange rates and current account deficits... But don't expect the presidency to put this on the agenda with the aim of getting results," he said.  \par \par \uc2 TAX EVASION, DEBT WORKOUTS  \par \par \uc2 The source said he expected ministers, including ones from oil producers Russia, Saudi Arabia, Mexico and Indonesia, to discuss the current situation on oil markets.  \par \par \uc2 Current account imbalances, particularly the U.S. trade deficit, would also play a role, he said.  \par \par \uc2 The G20's formal agenda will range from an assessment of the global economic outlook to combating money laundering, a German finance ministry spokesman told a government news conference on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The source repeated Germany hoped G20 nations would sign up to an Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development (OECD) code on exchanging information on tax matters.  \par \par \uc2 He also said he hoped the G20 would give backing to a voluntary code of conduct on sovereign debt crisis resolution that is being drawn up jointly by the banking industry and debtor nations.  \par \par \uc2 The G20 comprises the Group of Seven (G7) rich nations and big emerging market economies such as China, India and Brazil.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041117e0bh00a4f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
